WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.903
This is All in a Row: Compressed Convolution
Networks for Graphs,

00:00:04.983 --> 00:00:09.197
an ICML 2023 paper from the Chinese Academy of Sciences.

00:00:09.277 --> 00:00:14.717
Can we run standard, CNN-style Euclidean
convolution directly on graphs?

00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:19.777
Yes: learn a differentiable permutation that lines
nodes in a row,

00:00:19.857 --> 00:00:22.230
then slide a kernel across them.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.220
The model, CoCN, sets state of the art.
